    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **261 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including both new acceptance tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field derived from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, else UNKNOWN), returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing derived-field pattern (`membershipTier`, `displayName`, `initials`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` plus a `locality(Owner)` default method backed by a fixed `CITY_REGION` map, returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n\nThe endpoint is served through the existing OfficeFloor pipeline (`LoadOwner` \u2192 `RespondWithOwner`), which already delegates DTO construction to `OwnerMapper`, so no new function classes or YAML were needed \u2014 the derivation happens at read-time mapping.",
